1
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:15,080
Well struck.

2
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:16,870
Well struck, Dog.

3
00:02:21,510 --> 00:02:22,650
Did you like that?

4
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:25,010
It was well struck, Your Grace.

5
00:02:25,020 --> 00:02:26,680
I already said it was well struck.

6
00:02:28,510 --> 00:02:29,680
Yes, Your Grace.

7
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:39,410
Who's next?

8
00:02:39,410 --> 00:02:40,450
Lothor Brune,

9
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:43,240
freerider in the service of Lord Baelish.

10
00:02:43,870 --> 00:02:46,980
Ser Dontos the Red of House Hollard.

11
00:02:49,890 --> 00:02:52,580
Ser Dontos the Red of House Hollard!

12
00:02:52,980 --> 00:02:53,890
Here I am.

13
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:55,430
Here I am.

14
00:03:02,670 --> 00:03:03,860
Sorry, Your Grace.

15
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:06,490
My deepest apologies.

16
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:09,020
- Are you drunk? - No.

17
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:10,740
Uh, no. No, Your Grace.

18
00:03:10,750 --> 00:03:14,130
- I had two cups of wine. - Two cups?

19
00:03:14,430 --> 00:03:15,740
That's not much at all.

20
00:03:16,770 --> 00:03:18,660
Please, have another cup.

21
00:03:19,140 --> 00:03:20,180
Are you sure, Your Grace?

22
00:03:20,190 --> 00:03:22,830
Yes. To celebrate my name day.

23
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:24,960
Have two. Have as much as you like.

24
00:03:26,630 --> 00:03:28,260
I would be honored, Your Grace.

25
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:32,110
Ser Meryn, help Ser Dontos celebrate my name day.

26
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:35,210
See that he drinks his fill.

27
00:03:53,550 --> 00:03:54,970
You can't.

28
00:03:55,830 --> 00:03:56,880
What did you say?

29
00:03:58,750 --> 00:04:00,180
Did you say I can't?

30
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:03,360
I only meant it would be bad luck

31
00:04:03,370 --> 00:04:05,080
to kill a man on your name day.

32
00:04:05,270 --> 00:04:07,910
What kind of stupid peasant's superstition...

33
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:09,200
The girl is right.

34
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:11,220
What a man sows on his name day

35
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:12,550
he reaps all year.

36
00:04:16,570 --> 00:04:17,470
Take him away.

37
00:04:17,850 --> 00:04:20,110
I'll have him killed tomorrow, the fool.

38
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:24,730
He is.

39
00:04:24,740 --> 00:04:26,820
A fool-- you're so clever to see it.

40
00:04:27,380 --> 00:04:29,420
He'll make a much better fool than a knight.

41
00:04:29,660 --> 00:04:31,810
He doesn't deserve the mercy of a quick death.

42
00:04:34,570 --> 00:04:36,640
Did you hear My Lady, Ser Dontos?

43
00:04:37,310 --> 00:04:40,020
From this day, you'll be my new fool.

44
00:04:40,820 --> 00:04:41,920
Thank you, Your Grace.

45
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:45,300
And you, My Lady, thank you.

46
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:47,510
Beloved nephew.

47
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:57,290
We looked for you on the battlefield.

48
00:04:59,850 --> 00:05:02,020
You were nowhere to be found.

49
00:05:03,790 --> 00:05:06,050
I've been here, ruling the kingdoms.

50
00:05:06,060 --> 00:05:08,220
What a fine job you've done.

51
00:05:09,780 --> 00:05:10,840
Look at you.

52
00:05:12,380 --> 00:05:14,040
More beautiful than ever.

53
00:05:14,550 --> 00:05:18,680
And you! You-- you're going to be bigger than the Hound,

54
00:05:18,690 --> 00:05:20,430
but much better looking.

55
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:22,610
This one doesn't like me.

56
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:24,350
Can't imagine why.

57
00:05:24,640 --> 00:05:26,320
We heard you were dead.

58
00:05:26,320 --> 00:05:27,680
I'm glad you're not dead.

59
00:05:28,670 --> 00:05:29,750
Me, too, dear.

60
00:05:29,760 --> 00:05:31,590
Death is so boring, especially now

61
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:33,520
with so much excitement in the world.

62
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:37,640
My Lady, I'm sorry for your loss.

63
00:05:38,790 --> 00:05:40,140
Her loss?

64
00:05:40,220 --> 00:05:42,210
Her father was a confessed traitor.

65
00:05:42,220 --> 00:05:43,720
But still her father.

66
00:05:43,730 --> 00:05:45,640
Surely having so recently lost your own beloved father

67
00:05:45,650 --> 00:05:47,340
you can sympathize.

68
00:05:51,900 --> 00:05:53,550
My father was a traitor.

69
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:56,060
My mother and brother are traitors, too.

70
00:05:56,070 --> 00:05:58,370
I am loyal to my beloved Joffrey.

71
00:05:59,970 --> 00:06:01,200
Of course you are.

72
00:06:04,150 --> 00:06:07,810
Well, enjoy your name day, Your Grace.

73
00:06:08,230 --> 00:06:10,110
Wish I could stay and celebrate,

74
00:06:10,330 --> 00:06:12,820
but there is work to be done.

75
00:06:12,830 --> 00:06:13,820
What work?

76
00:06:14,970 --> 00:06:16,000
Why are you here?

77
00:06:20,450 --> 00:06:25,440
The raven arrived from the Citadel this morning, Your Grace.

78
00:06:26,190 --> 00:06:29,100
The conclave has met, considered reports

79
00:06:29,110 --> 00:06:31,830
from Maesters all over the Seven Kingdoms,

80
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:37,370
and declared this great summer done at last.

81
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:40,160
The longest summer in living memory.

82
00:06:40,670 --> 00:06:42,880
The peasants say, a long summer means

83
00:06:42,890 --> 00:06:45,750
- an even longer winter. - A common superstition.

84
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:48,020
We have enough wheat for a five-year winter.

85
00:06:48,390 --> 00:06:49,910
If it lasts any longer,

86
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:52,630
we'll have fewer peasants.

87
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:56,870
The city's drowning in refugees, Your Grace, fleeing the war.

88
00:06:56,880 --> 00:06:58,070
We have nowhere to house them.

89
00:06:58,080 --> 00:06:59,860
And with winter coming, it'll only get worse.

90
00:07:00,010 --> 00:07:02,860
You command the City Watch, do you not, Lord Slynt?

91
00:07:04,710 --> 00:07:05,780
I do, Your Grace.

92
00:07:06,490 --> 00:07:08,470
And are you not a Lord at my command?

93
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:11,950
I owe my title and lands to your generosity, Your Grace.

94
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:14,380
Then do your job. Shut the gates to the peasants.

95
00:07:14,390 --> 00:07:17,180
They belong in the field, not our capital.

96
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:18,690
Yes, Your Grace.

97
00:07:26,300 --> 00:07:27,280
Don't get up.

98
00:07:28,710 --> 00:07:31,660
More ravishing than ever, big sister.

99
00:07:33,700 --> 00:07:35,340
War agrees with you.

100
00:07:36,220 --> 00:07:39,110
Forgive the interruption. Carry on.

101
00:07:40,570 --> 00:07:41,850
What are you doing here?

102
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:45,790
Ah, it's been a remarkable journey.

103
00:07:46,050 --> 00:07:49,370
I pissed off the edge of the Wall,

104
00:07:49,980 --> 00:07:51,820
I slept in a sky cell,

105
00:07:52,190 --> 00:07:53,990
I fought with the hill tribes...

106
00:07:54,460 --> 00:07:55,890
so many adventures,

107
00:07:57,260 --> 00:07:59,530
so much to be thankful for.

108
00:08:00,110 --> 00:08:03,680
What are you doing here? This is the small council.

109
00:08:03,760 --> 00:08:06,480
Yes. Well I, do believe, the Hand of the King,

110
00:08:06,490 --> 00:08:08,520
is welcome at all small council meetings.

111
00:08:08,590 --> 00:08:10,450
Our father is Hand of the King.

112
00:08:10,580 --> 00:08:13,130
Yes, but in his absence...

113
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:22,960
Your father has named Lord Tyrion

114
00:08:22,970 --> 00:08:25,900
to serve as Hand in his stead while he fights.

115
00:08:25,910 --> 00:08:27,520
Out! All of you out!

116
00:08:33,410 --> 00:08:36,080
I would like to know how you tricked father into this.

117
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:37,910
If I were capable of tricking father,

118
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:39,780
I'd be emperor of the world by now.

119
00:08:40,040 --> 00:08:41,770
You brought this on yourself.

120
00:08:42,610 --> 00:08:43,560
I've done nothing.

121
00:08:43,570 --> 00:08:45,330
Quite right-- you did nothing

122
00:08:45,510 --> 00:08:47,670
when your son called for Ned Stark's head.

123
00:08:47,740 --> 00:08:49,830
Now the entire North has risen up against us.

124
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:52,510
- I tried to stop it. - Did you? You failed.

125
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:55,440
That bit of theater will haunt our family for a generation.

126
00:08:55,450 --> 00:08:56,820
Robb Stark is a child.

127
00:08:56,820 --> 00:08:59,600
Who's won every battle he's fought.

128
00:09:00,190 --> 00:09:02,470
Do you understand we're losing the war?

129
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:04,510
- What do you know about warfare? - Nothing.

130
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:06,460
But I know people.

131
00:09:07,050 --> 00:09:08,700
And I know that our enemies hate each other

132
00:09:08,710 --> 00:09:11,030
almost as much as they hate us.

133
00:09:16,590 --> 00:09:19,090
- Joffrey is King. - Joffrey is King.

134
00:09:19,750 --> 00:09:21,350
You are here to advise him.

135
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:23,140
I'm only here to advise him.

136
00:09:23,710 --> 00:09:25,720
And if the King listens to what I say,

137
00:09:25,730 --> 00:09:29,330
the King might just get his Uncle Jaime back.

138
00:09:31,170 --> 00:09:32,270
How?

139
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:33,660
You love your children.

140
00:09:34,140 --> 00:09:35,620
It's your one redeeming quality.

141
00:09:35,630 --> 00:09:36,920
That and your cheekbones.

142
00:09:38,700 --> 00:09:40,520
The Starks love their children as well.

143
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:43,700
- And we have two of them. - One.

144
00:09:46,030 --> 00:09:48,710
- One? - Arya, little animal... she disappeared.

145
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:51,360
Disappeared? What, in a puff of smoke?

146
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:56,510
We had three Starks to trade.

147
00:09:56,800 --> 00:09:59,700
You chopped one's head off and let another escape.

148
00:10:00,330 --> 00:10:01,910
Father will be furious.

149
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,140
It must be odd for you...

150
00:10:07,830 --> 00:10:09,550
to be the disappointing child.

151
00:10:17,870 --> 00:10:21,400
My Lord, may the Old Gods watch over your brother

152
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:23,710
and all our northern sons.

153
00:10:24,220 --> 00:10:27,890
The walls of my holdfast will not stand the winter.

154
00:10:28,140 --> 00:10:31,790
The stones were last mortared in the time of King Aerys,

155
00:10:32,380 --> 00:10:34,540
and I'm afraid the masons today

156
00:10:34,550 --> 00:10:37,230
are not fit to carry their fathers' hammers.

157
00:10:38,270 --> 00:10:40,660
When I was a boy, I remember seeing them

158
00:10:40,670 --> 00:10:45,200
put up a new tower at Torrhen's Square in a summer.

159
00:10:45,340 --> 00:10:46,910
Men worked back then.

160
00:10:47,450 --> 00:10:51,730
Today, my Holdfast looks like it was built by drunk children.

161
00:10:53,030 --> 00:10:57,130
At night you can hear the wind howling through the gaps.

162
00:10:57,460 --> 00:10:59,370
And the Gods forbid it rains.

163
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:02,190
Why, I might as well sleep beneath a waterfall.

164
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:04,280
Maintenance of a Holdfast

165
00:11:04,290 --> 00:11:07,190
generally falls to the lord of that Holdfast.

166
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:08,660
Generally, yes,

167
00:11:08,670 --> 00:11:10,400
but I've sent all the young men off

168
00:11:10,410 --> 00:11:12,410
to fight Robb Stark's war.

169
00:11:12,420 --> 00:11:14,940
King Robb. And it's not his war.

170
00:11:15,830 --> 00:11:17,090
He didn't choose it.

171
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:18,540
Maybe not, My Lord,

172
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:21,030
but he called in his Banners and took the men.

173
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:22,700
Joffrey killed my father,

174
00:11:23,410 --> 00:11:24,620
your liege lord.

175
00:11:25,460 --> 00:11:27,410
Do you remember your vows, Ser?

176
00:11:27,950 --> 00:11:29,780
Of course I remember!

177
00:11:29,790 --> 00:11:32,800
We can spare four masons for a week, My Lord.

178
00:11:32,810 --> 00:11:35,420
Will that be sufficient to repair your walls?

179
00:11:36,250 --> 00:11:37,870
I... I believe it will.

180
00:11:44,140 --> 00:11:46,110
We didn't want him here all day, did we?

181
00:11:47,940 --> 00:11:49,830
I didn't like the way he was talking about Robb.

182
00:11:50,900 --> 00:11:51,850
Nor did I.

183
00:11:55,090 --> 00:11:57,540
But listening to people you'd rather not listen to

184
00:11:57,550 --> 00:12:01,220
is one of your responsibilities as Lord of Winterfell.

185
00:12:05,330 --> 00:12:06,300
Lord Portan.

186
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:10,040
My Lord, may the Old Gods watch over your brother

187
00:12:10,050 --> 00:12:11,830
and all our northern sons.

188
00:13:01,150 --> 00:13:04,210
Boil this for an hour and drink the tea.

189
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:07,180
Makes all your pain go away.

190
00:13:08,030 --> 00:13:09,640
Don't have any pain.

191
00:13:10,460 --> 00:13:11,490
Lucky for you.

192
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:14,110
That way.

193
00:13:18,020 --> 00:13:19,790
You've been having those dreams again.

194
00:13:20,290 --> 00:13:21,190
I don't dream.

195
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:23,310
Everyone dreams.

196
00:13:23,730 --> 00:13:24,680
I don't.

197
00:13:26,510 --> 00:13:28,650
Heard some of the men talking about the comet.

198
00:13:29,230 --> 00:13:30,250
They say it's an omen.

199
00:13:30,830 --> 00:13:33,770
They say it means Robb will win a great victory in the South.

200
00:13:34,150 --> 00:13:35,070
Did they?

201
00:13:37,990 --> 00:13:40,900
I heard some other fools say it's Lannister Red.

202
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:44,290
Means the Lannisters will rule all Seven Kingdoms before long.

203
00:13:45,230 --> 00:13:47,970
Heard a stableboy say it's the color of blood

204
00:13:48,270 --> 00:13:49,830
to mark the death of your father.

205
00:13:54,620 --> 00:13:56,720
The stars don't fall for men.

206
00:13:57,860 --> 00:13:59,860
The red comet means one thing, boy--

207
00:14:01,770 --> 00:14:02,820
dragons.

208
00:14:05,060 --> 00:14:06,410
The dragons are all dead.

209
00:14:07,820 --> 00:14:09,370
They've been dead for centuries.

210
00:14:53,620 --> 00:14:55,950
What did your brother say about them, Khaleesi?

211
00:14:56,090 --> 00:14:57,840
He said they ate meat.

212
00:14:57,960 --> 00:14:59,830
He didn't tell you what kind of meat?

213
00:15:01,690 --> 00:15:03,850
My brother didn't know anything about dragons.

214
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:06,970
He didn't know anything about anything.

215
00:15:41,430 --> 00:15:43,400
She was Drogo's first gift to me.

216
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:45,660
I remember.

217
00:15:48,680 --> 00:15:50,660
I promised to protect them.

218
00:15:51,210 --> 00:15:53,400
Promised them their enemies would die screaming.

219
00:15:53,410 --> 00:15:55,350
How do I make starvation scream?

220
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:58,210
A trick I never learned, I'm afraid.

221
00:16:00,790 --> 00:16:02,050
Does it ever end?

222
00:16:02,980 --> 00:16:04,940
This is further east than I've ever been.

223
00:16:04,950 --> 00:16:06,660
But, yes, Khaleesi,

224
00:16:06,670 --> 00:16:08,390
everything ends, even the red waste.

225
00:16:08,400 --> 00:16:10,320
And you're sure there's no other way?

226
00:16:10,750 --> 00:16:13,360
If we go south to the land of the Lazarheen,

227
00:16:13,370 --> 00:16:15,840
the Lamb Men will kill us and take your dragons.

228
00:16:15,850 --> 00:16:17,560
If we go west to the Dothraki Sea,

229
00:16:17,570 --> 00:16:19,410
the first Khalasar we meet

230
00:16:19,730 --> 00:16:21,290
will kill us and take your dragons.

231
00:16:21,300 --> 00:16:23,920
No one will take my dragons.

232
00:16:25,110 --> 00:16:26,770
They are too weak to fight,

233
00:16:27,930 --> 00:16:29,440
as are your people.

234
00:16:30,160 --> 00:16:31,770
You must be their strength.

235
00:16:33,300 --> 00:16:34,500
As you are mine.

236
00:17:22,530 --> 00:17:23,760
Rakharo...

237
00:17:32,830 --> 00:17:34,170
You never have.

238
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:42,900
This is bad time to start.

239
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:40,970
Having a rough time of it?

240
00:18:41,550 --> 00:18:43,050
Nothing's killed me yet.

241
00:18:43,140 --> 00:18:45,610
- Your ass killed the sledge. - You offered me a ride.

242
00:18:45,620 --> 00:18:48,210
I just wanted you to shut up about your damn blisters.

243
00:19:02,960 --> 00:19:04,970
I was born in a place like this.

244
00:19:05,970 --> 00:19:08,300
Later, I fell on hard times.

245
00:19:10,550 --> 00:19:11,870
Are those girls?

246
00:19:12,490 --> 00:19:13,880
Craster's daughters.

247
00:19:15,010 --> 00:19:17,400
I haven't seen a girl in six months.

248
00:19:18,190 --> 00:19:20,510
I'd keep on not seeing them if I were you.

249
00:19:20,950 --> 00:19:23,300
What, he don't like people messing with his daughters?

250
00:19:23,310 --> 00:19:25,620
He don't like people messing with his wives.

251
00:19:28,390 --> 00:19:30,080
He marries his daughters,

252
00:19:30,090 --> 00:19:31,720
and they give him more daughters.

253
00:19:31,730 --> 00:19:33,910
And on and on it goes.

254
00:19:34,510 --> 00:19:36,750
- That's foul. - It's beyond foul.

255
00:19:36,760 --> 00:19:39,800
All the other wildlings for a hundred leagues have disappeared.

256
00:19:40,830 --> 00:19:42,020
Craster's still here.

257
00:19:42,930 --> 00:19:44,780
He must be doing something right.

258
00:19:47,130 --> 00:19:48,500
What happens to the boys?

259
00:19:49,150 --> 00:19:51,780
- Hmm? - He marries his daughters.

260
00:19:52,570 --> 00:19:54,140
What does he do with his sons?

261
00:19:57,430 --> 00:19:59,380
He said he planned to stop here

262
00:19:59,420 --> 00:20:01,120
on his way to the Frostfangs.

263
00:20:01,300 --> 00:20:03,090
People make all sorts of plans.

264
00:20:03,100 --> 00:20:06,600
I haven't seen Benjen Stark in three years.

265
00:20:06,690 --> 00:20:07,920
Haven't missed him.

266
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:09,960
Always treated me like scum.

267
00:20:11,980 --> 00:20:14,460
Haven't had any good wine for a long time.

268
00:20:14,750 --> 00:20:17,750
You Southerners make good wine, I'll give you that.

269
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:19,050
We're not Southerners.

270
00:20:19,790 --> 00:20:21,140
Who's this little girl?

271
00:20:23,090 --> 00:20:25,530
You're prettier than half my daughters.

272
00:20:25,770 --> 00:20:28,530
You got a nice wet twat between your legs?

273
00:20:29,140 --> 00:20:30,040
What's your name?

274
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:32,700
- Jon Snow. - Snow, eh?

275
00:20:33,250 --> 00:20:35,180
Listen to me, bastard.

276
00:20:35,970 --> 00:20:39,390
All you lot from south of the Wall, you're Southerners.

277
00:20:40,140 --> 00:20:44,150
But now you're in the North, the real North.

278
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:45,450
The lad meant no harm.

279
00:20:47,220 --> 00:20:50,230
I catch that pretty little bastard talking to my daughters...

280
00:20:50,240 --> 00:20:53,870
No one will talk to your daughters, you have my word.

281
00:20:54,440 --> 00:20:57,460
Now, sit down and shut your mouth.

282
00:21:00,640 --> 00:21:02,950
You bring any of that good wine with you?

283
00:21:02,960 --> 00:21:03,970
We did.

284
00:21:04,370 --> 00:21:07,050
We passed through six villages on the way here.

285
00:21:07,060 --> 00:21:09,460
All six were abandoned.

286
00:21:09,980 --> 00:21:11,580
Where have all the wildlings gone?

287
00:21:12,080 --> 00:21:14,670
I could tell you, but I'm thirsty.

288
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:17,840
There's a barrel of Dornish wine on the sledge.

289
00:21:17,850 --> 00:21:20,100
- Bring it in here. - Yes, commander.

290
00:21:20,600 --> 00:21:23,080
You want to know where they've all gone?

291
00:21:23,410 --> 00:21:27,470
North... to join up with Mance Rayder...

292
00:21:29,460 --> 00:21:30,460
Your old friend.

293
00:21:31,470 --> 00:21:33,000
He's no friend of mine.

294
00:21:33,670 --> 00:21:36,750
He broke his vows, betrayed his brothers.

295
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:37,990
Oh, aye.

296
00:21:38,100 --> 00:21:40,700
But once he was just a poor black crow.

297
00:21:40,890 --> 00:21:43,560
And now he's King-Beyond-the-Wall.

298
00:21:44,210 --> 00:21:46,520
He's been calling himself that for years.

299
00:21:46,630 --> 00:21:49,910
What's he king of? A frozen lake somewhere?

300
00:21:51,860 --> 00:21:53,490
That's a good-looking axe.

301
00:21:53,950 --> 00:21:55,270
Fresh forged?

302
00:21:58,160 --> 00:21:59,040
Give it here.

303
00:22:00,680 --> 00:22:02,740
You'll have another one made at Castle Black.

304
00:22:02,820 --> 00:22:03,820
Here.

305
00:22:06,340 --> 00:22:08,240
Oh, that's some lovely steel.

306
00:22:12,310 --> 00:22:14,570
You want to know what Mance Rayder is doing?

307
00:22:15,440 --> 00:22:16,810
Gathering an army.

308
00:22:17,650 --> 00:22:19,420
What I hear, he's already got more men

309
00:22:19,430 --> 00:22:21,250
than any of your southern kings.

310
00:22:21,260 --> 00:22:24,220
And where does he plan marching this army?

311
00:22:24,310 --> 00:22:25,680
When you're all the way north,

312
00:22:25,690 --> 00:22:27,400
there's only one direction to go.

313
00:22:29,960 --> 00:22:33,740
These are bad times to be living alone in the wild.

314
00:22:34,720 --> 00:22:36,260
The cold winds are rising.

315
00:22:37,830 --> 00:22:40,900
Let them come. My roots are sunk deep.

316
00:22:42,780 --> 00:22:43,700
Wife...

317
00:22:44,930 --> 00:22:48,810
tell the Lord Crow how content we are.

318
00:22:49,420 --> 00:22:50,770
This is our place.

319
00:22:51,310 --> 00:22:53,360
Our husband keeps us safe.

320
00:22:53,580 --> 00:22:55,950
Better to live free than die a slave.

321
00:22:59,010 --> 00:23:01,040
Don't it make you jealous, old man,

322
00:23:02,050 --> 00:23:03,810
to see me with all these young wives

323
00:23:03,820 --> 00:23:05,820
and you with no one to warm your bed?

324
00:23:07,170 --> 00:23:09,120
We chose different paths.

325
00:23:09,130 --> 00:23:13,310
Oh, aye, and you chose the path with no one but boys on it.

326
00:23:15,530 --> 00:23:18,660
You'll be wanting to sleep beneath my roof, I suppose,

327
00:23:18,990 --> 00:23:20,590
and eat me out of pigs.

328
00:23:20,780 --> 00:23:22,280
A roof would be welcome.

329
00:23:22,670 --> 00:23:23,920
It's been hard riding.

330
00:23:24,170 --> 00:23:27,170
We've brought our own food and good steel for you.

331
00:23:30,270 --> 00:23:33,300
Any man lays a hand on one of my wives,

332
00:23:33,760 --> 00:23:35,480
he loses the hand.

333
00:23:37,790 --> 00:23:41,050
And I see this one staring too long,

334
00:23:41,580 --> 00:23:43,590
I might just gouge his eyes out.

335
00:23:44,640 --> 00:23:47,580
Your roof, your rules.

336
00:24:00,850 --> 00:24:02,090
Who am I?!

337
00:24:03,410 --> 00:24:06,690
- Who am I?! - Lord commander.

338
00:24:06,960 --> 00:24:09,900
- And who are you? - Jon Snow.

339
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:11,480
Who are you?

340
00:24:12,930 --> 00:24:13,900
Your steward.

341
00:24:14,840 --> 00:24:16,360
You want to lead one day?

342
00:24:20,010 --> 00:24:21,630
Then learn how to follow.

343
00:24:39,700 --> 00:24:43,730
Lord of Light, come to us in our darkness.

344
00:24:44,480 --> 00:24:47,580
We offer you these false Gods.

345
00:24:48,100 --> 00:24:51,020
Take them and cast your light upon us...

346
00:24:53,150 --> 00:24:56,480
For the night is dark and full of terrors.

347
00:24:57,250 --> 00:25:00,770
For the night is dark and full of terrors.

348
00:25:02,850 --> 00:25:04,840
After the long summer,

349
00:25:04,850 --> 00:25:07,520
darkness will fall heavy on the world.

350
00:25:07,620 --> 00:25:09,740
The stars will bleed.

351
00:25:10,940 --> 00:25:12,920
We need to stop her.

352
00:25:13,040 --> 00:25:16,920
The cold breath of winter will freeze the seas...

353
00:25:17,400 --> 00:25:18,170
Not now.

354
00:25:18,180 --> 00:25:20,760
And the dead shall rise in the North.

355
00:25:22,870 --> 00:25:26,010
All you men were named in the Light of the Seven!

356
00:25:26,540 --> 00:25:29,860
Is this how you treat the Gods of your fathers?

357
00:25:29,860 --> 00:25:34,030
Are you so eager to spit on your ancestors?

358
00:25:43,130 --> 00:25:44,550
You smell of fear--

359
00:25:45,410 --> 00:25:49,390
fear and piss and old bones.

360
00:25:50,920 --> 00:25:52,300
Do you want to stop me?

361
00:25:57,050 --> 00:25:58,040
Stop me.

362
00:26:11,820 --> 00:26:13,490
In the ancient books, it's written

363
00:26:13,500 --> 00:26:17,110
that a warrior will draw a burning sword from the fire.

364
00:26:18,520 --> 00:26:21,150
And that sword shall be Lightbringer.

365
00:26:26,670 --> 00:26:28,960
Stannis Baratheon,

366
00:26:30,250 --> 00:26:32,010
warrior of light,

367
00:26:32,750 --> 00:26:34,290
your sword awaits you.

368
00:27:05,200 --> 00:27:08,290
Lord, cast your light upon us!

369
00:27:09,950 --> 00:27:13,370
For the night is dark and full of terrors.

370
00:27:16,130 --> 00:27:18,670
For the night is dark and full of terror.

371
00:27:46,290 --> 00:27:49,970
This woman will lead him into a war he cannot win.

372
00:27:49,970 --> 00:27:51,280
Stannis is our king.

373
00:27:52,110 --> 00:27:53,390
We follow where he leads,

374
00:27:53,390 --> 00:27:55,270
- even if we don't like the path. - King.

375
00:27:56,380 --> 00:27:58,220
Since that boar killed his brother,

376
00:27:58,220 --> 00:27:59,880
every lord wants a coronation.

377
00:28:00,030 --> 00:28:02,540
I don't serve the others. I serve Stannis.

378
00:28:02,540 --> 00:28:05,800
As do I, but loyal service

379
00:28:06,210 --> 00:28:07,920
means telling hard truths.

380
00:28:08,920 --> 00:28:11,700
He's surrounded by fools and fanatics,

381
00:28:12,860 --> 00:28:15,310
but he trusts you, Davos.

382
00:28:16,150 --> 00:28:18,020
If you tell him the truth...

383
00:28:20,850 --> 00:28:21,840
What's the truth?

384
00:28:35,040 --> 00:28:36,930
"And I declare upon the honor of my house

385
00:28:36,930 --> 00:28:38,200
that my beloved brother Robert--"

386
00:28:38,200 --> 00:28:39,680
he wasn't my beloved brother.

387
00:28:40,810 --> 00:28:43,310
I didn't love him. He didn't love me.

388
00:28:43,550 --> 00:28:44,970
A harmless courtesy, Your Grace.

389
00:28:44,970 --> 00:28:46,270
A lie. Take it out.

390
00:28:49,230 --> 00:28:51,510
"...that my brother Robert left no trueborn heirs,

391
00:28:51,830 --> 00:28:53,750
the boy Joffrey, the boy Tommen,

392
00:28:53,750 --> 00:28:55,610
and the girl Myrcella being born of incest

393
00:28:55,610 --> 00:28:58,560
between Cersei Lannister and her brother Jaime Lannister.

394
00:28:59,080 --> 00:29:00,320
By right of birth--"

395
00:29:00,320 --> 00:29:01,660
Jaime Lannister, the Kingslayer.

396
00:29:01,920 --> 00:29:02,780
Call him what he is.

397
00:29:05,170 --> 00:29:07,440
"...And her brother Jaime Lannister, the Kingslayer.

398
00:29:07,850 --> 00:29:11,270
By right of birth and blood, I do this day lay claim--"

399
00:29:11,270 --> 00:29:13,490
Make it Ser Jaime Lannister, the Kingslayer.

400
00:29:14,260 --> 00:29:15,950
Whatever else he is, the man's still a knight.

401
00:29:16,190 --> 00:29:18,100
"Ser Jaime Lannister, the Kingslayer.

402
00:29:18,750 --> 00:29:20,510
By right of birth and blood,

403
00:29:20,750 --> 00:29:21,980
I do this day lay claim

404
00:29:21,980 --> 00:29:23,450
to the Iron Throne of Westeros.

405
00:29:24,450 --> 00:29:26,240
Let all true men declare their loyalty."

406
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:28,990
When Eddard Stark learned the truth, he told only me.

407
00:29:28,990 --> 00:29:30,480
I'll not make the same mistake.

408
00:29:31,550 --> 00:29:33,530
Send copies of that letter to every corner of the Realm,

409
00:29:33,530 --> 00:29:34,730
from the Arbor to the Wall.

410
00:29:35,860 --> 00:29:37,160
The time has come to choose.

411
00:29:38,750 --> 00:29:41,080
Let no man claim ignorance as an excuse.

412
00:29:41,080 --> 00:29:43,610
Your Grace, the Lannisters are the true enemy.

413
00:29:43,610 --> 00:29:45,710
If, for the time being, you could make peace with your brother--

414
00:29:45,710 --> 00:29:48,040
I'll not make peace with Renly while he calls himself King.

415
00:29:48,040 --> 00:29:49,760
Well, many have already declared for him--

416
00:29:49,760 --> 00:29:51,650
Mace Tyrell, Randyll Tarly.

417
00:29:51,850 --> 00:29:55,570
Stannis does not need to beg this lord or that lord for support.

418
00:29:55,570 --> 00:29:57,240
The Lord of Light stands behind him.

419
00:29:57,240 --> 00:29:59,970
And how many ships has the Lord of Light got in his fleet?

420
00:30:00,420 --> 00:30:02,630
- He has no need for ships. - I'm sure he doesn't,

421
00:30:02,930 --> 00:30:04,320
but we do if we're going to war.

422
00:30:04,940 --> 00:30:06,290
If not Renly, Your Grace,

423
00:30:06,290 --> 00:30:07,520
join forces with Robb Stark.

424
00:30:07,830 --> 00:30:09,840
Who would steal the northern half of my kingdom.

425
00:30:09,840 --> 00:30:11,720
I've always served thieves according to their desserts,

426
00:30:11,720 --> 00:30:13,220
as you well know, Ser Davos.

427
00:30:13,370 --> 00:30:15,650
Joffrey, Renly, Robb Stark, they're all thieves.

428
00:30:16,620 --> 00:30:18,420
They'll bend the knee or I'll destroy them.

429
00:30:20,030 --> 00:30:22,610
I owe you an apology, my King.

430
00:30:23,510 --> 00:30:25,270
My duty is to serve.

431
00:30:25,780 --> 00:30:29,500
You have chosen the new God over the Old Gods.

432
00:30:29,830 --> 00:30:32,450
May the Lord of Light watch over us all.

433
00:30:33,510 --> 00:30:35,100
Shall we drink together?

434
00:30:36,060 --> 00:30:36,730
Don't.

435
00:30:37,720 --> 00:30:41,630
A cup of wine to honor the one true God.

436
00:31:28,750 --> 00:31:31,190
The night is dark and full of terrors, old man,

437
00:31:32,330 --> 00:31:34,350
but the fire burns them all away.

438
00:31:56,780 --> 00:31:57,860
Your Grace.

439
00:32:09,830 --> 00:32:11,790
King in the North.

440
00:32:14,510 --> 00:32:18,410
I keep expecting you to leave me in one castle or another for safekeeping,

441
00:32:18,410 --> 00:32:21,330
but you drag me along from camp to camp.

442
00:32:23,140 --> 00:32:25,180
Have you grown fond of me, Stark?

443
00:32:25,180 --> 00:32:26,270
Is that it?

444
00:32:27,130 --> 00:32:28,590
I've never seen you with a girl.

445
00:32:30,200 --> 00:32:32,120
If I left you with one of my bannermen,

446
00:32:32,700 --> 00:32:34,600
your father would know within a fortnight

447
00:32:36,030 --> 00:32:38,380
and my bannerman would receive a raven with a message:

448
00:32:39,550 --> 00:32:42,820
"Release my son and you'll be rich beyond your dreams.

449
00:32:42,820 --> 00:32:46,050
Refuse and your house will be destroyed, root and stem."

450
00:32:46,650 --> 00:32:50,650
You don't trust the loyalty of the men following you into battle?

451
00:32:50,990 --> 00:32:52,600
Oh, I trust them with my life,

452
00:32:54,510 --> 00:32:56,030
just not with yours.

453
00:32:56,360 --> 00:32:57,550
Smart boy.

454
00:32:58,340 --> 00:32:59,490
What's wrong?

455
00:33:00,370 --> 00:33:02,020
Don't like being called "boy"?

456
00:33:02,820 --> 00:33:04,080
Insulted?

457
00:33:12,310 --> 00:33:14,300
You insult yourself, Kingslayer.

458
00:33:16,390 --> 00:33:18,660
You've been defeated by a boy.

459
00:33:20,220 --> 00:33:22,550
You're held captive by a boy.

460
00:33:25,100 --> 00:33:27,070
Perhaps you'll be killed by a boy.

461
00:33:33,680 --> 00:33:35,760
Stannis Baratheon sent ravens

462
00:33:35,760 --> 00:33:37,470
to all the high lords of Westeros.

463
00:33:39,220 --> 00:33:41,470
King Joffrey Baratheon

464
00:33:41,470 --> 00:33:44,480
is neither a true king nor a true Baratheon.

465
00:33:46,210 --> 00:33:47,720
He's your bastard son.

466
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:50,500
If that's true, Stannis is the rightful king.

467
00:33:50,500 --> 00:33:51,840
How convenient for him.

468
00:33:53,230 --> 00:33:56,250
My father learned the truth.

469
00:33:56,780 --> 00:33:58,190
That's why you had him executed.

470
00:33:58,200 --> 00:34:01,130
I was your prisoner when Ned Stark lost his head.

471
00:34:01,130 --> 00:34:02,840
Your son killed him

472
00:34:02,840 --> 00:34:04,720
so the world wouldn't learn who fathered him.

473
00:34:04,720 --> 00:34:08,560
And you... you pushed my brother from a window

474
00:34:08,560 --> 00:34:10,270
because he saw you with the queen.

475
00:34:15,520 --> 00:34:16,540
You have proof?

476
00:34:18,800 --> 00:34:21,130
Or do you want to trade gossip like a couple of fishwives?

477
00:34:21,130 --> 00:34:22,580
I'm sending one of your cousins down

478
00:34:22,580 --> 00:34:24,450
to King's Landing with my peace terms.

479
00:34:25,200 --> 00:34:27,390
You think my father's going to negotiate with you?

480
00:34:28,590 --> 00:34:30,060
You don't know him very well.

481
00:34:30,690 --> 00:34:33,820
No, but he's starting to know me.

482
00:34:35,490 --> 00:34:38,040
Three victories don't make you a conqueror.

483
00:34:40,160 --> 00:34:41,850
It's better than three defeats.

484
00:35:11,200 --> 00:35:12,570
This city stinks...

485
00:35:16,040 --> 00:35:17,530
Like dead bodies.

486
00:35:17,980 --> 00:35:19,480
A bit corpsey, yes.

487
00:35:20,550 --> 00:35:21,730
And shit.

488
00:35:22,540 --> 00:35:23,850
I thought you wanted to come here.

489
00:35:27,620 --> 00:35:28,920
I love it.

490
00:35:30,120 --> 00:35:32,470
You love the smell of dead bodies and shit?

491
00:35:33,960 --> 00:35:36,820
And cum and garlic and rum.

492
00:35:37,190 --> 00:35:38,700
You can smell cum from the balcony?

493
00:35:39,790 --> 00:35:42,800
I love the stink. I love the noise.

494
00:35:43,780 --> 00:35:45,420
Cities make me want to fuck.

495
00:35:46,370 --> 00:35:48,300
And so did the country.

496
00:35:51,860 --> 00:35:53,270
This is where I belong.

497
00:35:53,270 --> 00:35:55,600
Yes, well, you need to be careful.

498
00:35:56,510 --> 00:35:57,820
No one can know you're here.

499
00:35:57,820 --> 00:35:59,200
No one will know.

500
00:35:59,670 --> 00:36:01,280
You can't trust anyone in King's Landing.

501
00:36:01,280 --> 00:36:04,280
They're all liars-- good liars, bad liars,

502
00:36:04,620 --> 00:36:06,230
one or two great liars.

503
00:36:07,090 --> 00:36:08,280
What about you?

504
00:36:08,690 --> 00:36:11,710
Me? I'm not from here. I'm a slave to the truth.

505
00:36:13,360 --> 00:36:14,510
Truth?

506
00:36:16,030 --> 00:36:18,970
You are the biggest little liar I have ever met.

507
00:36:19,630 --> 00:36:21,280
Why do you think I am so little?

508
00:36:21,710 --> 00:36:25,500
I'm being crushed beneath the weight of all that truth.

509
00:36:30,250 --> 00:36:32,760
Ned Stark actually slept on this.

510
00:36:33,300 --> 00:36:36,110
As if the poor man didn't suffer enough.

511
00:36:38,670 --> 00:36:41,480
One of the many changes we'll have to make around here.

512
00:36:53,220 --> 00:36:56,590
- Lord Baelish. - Your Grace.

513
00:36:56,860 --> 00:36:58,980
I wonder if I might ask you for a favor.

514
00:36:59,400 --> 00:37:00,810
Of course, Your Grace.

515
00:37:00,810 --> 00:37:02,840
Ned Stark's youngest daughter Arya--

516
00:37:03,200 --> 00:37:04,760
we can't seem to locate her.

517
00:37:05,870 --> 00:37:07,470
If she's escaped the capital,

518
00:37:07,470 --> 00:37:09,580
Winterfell seems the logical destination.

519
00:37:09,580 --> 00:37:12,410
And yet my friends in the North report no sign of her.

520
00:37:12,730 --> 00:37:13,630
Curious.

521
00:37:14,310 --> 00:37:16,420
If we choose to negotiate with the Starks,

522
00:37:16,670 --> 00:37:18,500
the girl has some value. Whoever finds her--

523
00:37:18,510 --> 00:37:21,020
well, you know what they say about Lannisters and debts.

524
00:37:21,020 --> 00:37:23,350
Well, you could ask Varys where she is.

525
00:37:24,380 --> 00:37:25,590
He'll have an answer for you.

526
00:37:25,590 --> 00:37:26,850
Whether you believe it...

527
00:37:27,010 --> 00:37:30,570
Myself, I have always had a hard time trusting eunuchs.

528
00:37:31,260 --> 00:37:32,630
Who knows what they want?

529
00:37:33,910 --> 00:37:35,230
A mockingbird.

530
00:37:36,450 --> 00:37:38,730
You created your own Sigil, didn't you?

531
00:37:38,730 --> 00:37:39,570
Yes.

532
00:37:40,770 --> 00:37:42,760
Appropriate... for a self-made man

533
00:37:42,760 --> 00:37:44,380
with so many songs to sing.

534
00:37:44,750 --> 00:37:46,000
I'm glad you like it.

535
00:37:46,400 --> 00:37:48,210
Some people are fortunate enough

536
00:37:48,210 --> 00:37:49,760
to be born into the right family.

537
00:37:49,920 --> 00:37:52,140
Others have to find their own way.

538
00:37:53,860 --> 00:37:55,430
I heard a song once

539
00:37:55,880 --> 00:37:57,820
about a boy of modest means

540
00:37:59,140 --> 00:38:01,460
who found his way into the home of a very prominent family.

541
00:38:02,620 --> 00:38:04,000
He loved the eldest daughter.

542
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:06,840
Sadly, she had eyes for another.

543
00:38:07,950 --> 00:38:10,120
When boys and girls live in the same home,

544
00:38:10,120 --> 00:38:11,850
awkward situations can arise.

545
00:38:12,370 --> 00:38:13,950
Sometimes, I've heard,

546
00:38:13,950 --> 00:38:17,510
even brothers and sisters develop certain affections.

547
00:38:17,760 --> 00:38:20,130
And when these affections become common knowledge,

548
00:38:20,320 --> 00:38:24,200
well, that is an awkward situation indeed,

549
00:38:24,200 --> 00:38:25,960
especially in a prominent family.

550
00:38:26,490 --> 00:38:29,110
But prominent families often forget a simple truth,

551
00:38:29,670 --> 00:38:30,980
I've found.

552
00:38:32,710 --> 00:38:34,030
And which truth is that?

553
00:38:34,860 --> 00:38:37,070
Knowledge is power.

554
00:38:40,090 --> 00:38:41,440
Seize him.

555
00:38:44,900 --> 00:38:46,030
Cut his throat.

556
00:38:47,180 --> 00:38:48,340
Stop.

557
00:38:48,350 --> 00:38:49,510
Await.

558
00:38:50,270 --> 00:38:52,380
I've changed my mind. Let him go.

559
00:38:55,070 --> 00:38:56,690
Step back three paces.

560
00:38:58,500 --> 00:38:59,670
Turn around.

561
00:39:01,330 --> 00:39:02,430
Close your eyes.

562
00:39:06,580 --> 00:39:09,580
Power is power.

563
00:39:11,040 --> 00:39:14,600
Do see if you can take some time away from your coins and your whores

564
00:39:14,750 --> 00:39:16,670
to locate the Stark girl for me.

565
00:39:16,920 --> 00:39:18,710
I would very much appreciate it.

566
00:39:30,450 --> 00:39:31,850
You're Ser Alton Lannister?

567
00:39:33,040 --> 00:39:34,290
I am, Your Grace.

568
00:39:34,560 --> 00:39:38,190
I offer your cousins peace if they meet my terms.

569
00:39:38,470 --> 00:39:42,280
First, your family must release my sisters.

570
00:39:43,420 --> 00:39:46,500
Second, my father's bones must be returned to us

571
00:39:46,500 --> 00:39:48,510
so he may rest beside his brother and sister

572
00:39:48,510 --> 00:39:50,190
in the crypts beneath Winterfell.

573
00:39:50,950 --> 00:39:53,240
And the remains of all those who died in his service

574
00:39:53,250 --> 00:39:54,660
must also be returned.

575
00:39:55,820 --> 00:39:58,170
Their families can honor them with proper funerals.

576
00:39:58,420 --> 00:40:00,900
- An honorable request, Your Grace. - Third...

577
00:40:02,790 --> 00:40:05,470
Joffrey and the Queen Regent must renounce all claim

578
00:40:05,470 --> 00:40:06,720
to dominion of the North.

579
00:40:08,250 --> 00:40:10,380
From this time till the end of time,

580
00:40:10,380 --> 00:40:12,340
we are a free and independent kingdom.

581
00:40:12,870 --> 00:40:14,440
The King in the North.

582
00:40:14,770 --> 00:40:16,980
King in the North.

583
00:40:16,980 --> 00:40:19,000
Neither Joffrey nor any of his men

584
00:40:19,000 --> 00:40:20,820
shall set foot in our lands again.

585
00:40:21,270 --> 00:40:23,290
If he disregards this command,

586
00:40:23,510 --> 00:40:25,870
he shall suffer the same fate as my father,

587
00:40:26,800 --> 00:40:31,240
only I don't need a servant to do my beheading for me.

588
00:40:31,240 --> 00:40:34,730
These are-- Your Grace, these are--

589
00:40:34,730 --> 00:40:35,870
These are my terms.

590
00:40:37,420 --> 00:40:38,850
If the Queen Regent and her son meet them,

591
00:40:38,850 --> 00:40:40,080
I'll give them peace.

592
00:40:40,080 --> 00:40:41,220
If not...

593
00:40:43,290 --> 00:40:45,700
I will litter the south with Lannister dead.

594
00:40:45,950 --> 00:40:48,570
King Joffrey is a Baratheon, Your Grace.

595
00:40:48,570 --> 00:40:49,710
Oh, is he?

596
00:40:52,080 --> 00:40:53,830
You'll ride at daybreak, Ser Alton.

597
00:40:54,710 --> 00:40:56,210
That will be all for tonight.

598
00:41:12,270 --> 00:41:13,620
A word, Your Grace?

599
00:41:16,460 --> 00:41:18,900
You don't have to call me "Your Grace" when no one's around.

600
00:41:19,250 --> 00:41:21,790
It's not so bad once you get used to it.

601
00:41:22,040 --> 00:41:24,100
I'm glad someone's gotten used to it.

602
00:41:24,950 --> 00:41:27,140
The Lannisters are going to reject your terms, you know?

603
00:41:27,140 --> 00:41:28,300
Of course they are.

604
00:41:28,880 --> 00:41:30,980
We can fight them in the fields as long as you like,

605
00:41:31,580 --> 00:41:33,850
but we won't beat them until you take King's Landing.

606
00:41:36,810 --> 00:41:38,720
And we can't take King's Landing without ships.

607
00:41:39,840 --> 00:41:42,510
My father has ships and men who know how to sail them.

608
00:41:42,510 --> 00:41:44,100
Men who fought my father.

609
00:41:44,260 --> 00:41:45,400
Men who fought King Robert

610
00:41:45,400 --> 00:41:48,070
to free themselves from the yoke of the South,

611
00:41:48,070 --> 00:41:49,630
just like you're doing now.

612
00:41:51,740 --> 00:41:53,330
I'm his only living son.

613
00:41:54,530 --> 00:41:55,990
He'll listen to me.

614
00:41:56,370 --> 00:41:57,400
I know he will.

615
00:42:00,250 --> 00:42:02,140
I'm not a Stark. I know that.

616
00:42:03,770 --> 00:42:06,560
But your father raised me to be an honorable man.

617
00:42:08,530 --> 00:42:10,080
We can avenge him together.

618
00:42:12,680 --> 00:42:15,170
You don't want Balon Greyjoy for an ally.

619
00:42:15,170 --> 00:42:17,490
I need his ships. They say he has 200.

620
00:42:17,490 --> 00:42:21,210
They say a million rats live in the sewers of King's Landing.

621
00:42:21,210 --> 00:42:23,080
Shall we rally them to fight for us?

622
00:42:23,080 --> 00:42:24,960
I understand you don't trust Lord Greyjoy.

623
00:42:24,960 --> 00:42:28,490
I don't trust Lord Greyjoy because he is not trustworthy.

624
00:42:29,860 --> 00:42:32,370
Your father had to go to war to end his rebellion.

625
00:42:32,370 --> 00:42:33,350
Yes.

626
00:42:33,400 --> 00:42:35,610
And now I'm the one rebelling against the throne.

627
00:42:36,170 --> 00:42:37,630
Before me, it was father.

628
00:42:38,300 --> 00:42:40,420
You married one rebel and mothered another.

629
00:42:40,630 --> 00:42:42,580
I mothered more than just rebels,

630
00:42:43,120 --> 00:42:45,090
a fact you seem to have forgotten.

631
00:42:45,880 --> 00:42:47,910
If I trade the Kingslayer for two girls,

632
00:42:47,910 --> 00:42:49,880
my bannermen will string me up by my feet.

633
00:42:49,890 --> 00:42:52,520
You want to leave Sansa in the Queen's hands?

634
00:42:53,030 --> 00:42:54,060
And Arya...

635
00:42:55,150 --> 00:42:57,050
I haven't heard a word about Arya.

636
00:42:58,620 --> 00:43:00,140
What are we fighting for if not for them?

637
00:43:00,140 --> 00:43:01,520
It's more complicated than that!

638
00:43:01,520 --> 00:43:02,470
You know it is.

639
00:43:18,150 --> 00:43:19,800
It's time for me to go home.

640
00:43:21,780 --> 00:43:24,120
I haven't seen Bran or Rickon in months.

641
00:43:25,860 --> 00:43:27,430
You can't go to Winterfell.

642
00:43:29,170 --> 00:43:30,180
I beg your pardon?

643
00:43:30,680 --> 00:43:32,590
I'll send Rodrik to watch over the boys

644
00:43:33,900 --> 00:43:37,570
because tomorrow you'll ride south to the Stormlands.

645
00:43:38,670 --> 00:43:40,330
Why in the name of all the Gods...

646
00:43:40,330 --> 00:43:43,150
Because I need you to negotiate with Renly Baratheon.

647
00:43:44,200 --> 00:43:46,540
He's rallied an army of 100,000.

648
00:43:46,540 --> 00:43:48,310
You know him. You know his family.

649
00:43:48,310 --> 00:43:50,600
I haven't seen Renly Baratheon since he was a boy.

650
00:43:50,600 --> 00:43:52,020
You have a hundred other lords...

651
00:43:52,020 --> 00:43:54,250
Which of these lords do I trust more than you?

652
00:43:56,230 --> 00:43:57,770
If Renly sides with us,

653
00:43:58,780 --> 00:44:00,450
we'll outnumber them two to one.

654
00:44:01,480 --> 00:44:04,170
When they feel the jaws beginning to shut, they'll sue for peace.

655
00:44:04,340 --> 00:44:05,990
We'll get the girls back.

656
00:44:07,190 --> 00:44:09,810
Then we'll all go home... for good.

657
00:44:18,790 --> 00:44:20,500
I will ride at first light.

658
00:44:29,380 --> 00:44:32,070
We will all be together again soon, I promise.

659
00:44:38,050 --> 00:44:39,900
You've done so well.

660
00:44:41,810 --> 00:44:44,750
Your father would be... proud.

661
00:44:53,530 --> 00:44:56,090
- Give Lord Renly my regards. - King Renly.

662
00:44:58,060 --> 00:44:59,750
There's a king in every corner now.

663
00:45:13,730 --> 00:45:14,730
What is all this?

664
00:45:15,810 --> 00:45:18,090
Returning this room to its proper appearance.

665
00:45:18,540 --> 00:45:21,260
Say what you will about the Targaryens-- they were conquerors.

666
00:45:21,580 --> 00:45:23,710
That is a seat for a conqueror.

667
00:45:24,050 --> 00:45:27,080
It needs a room to match it, not vines and flowers.

668
00:45:27,800 --> 00:45:29,520
We can't find Arya Stark.

669
00:45:30,150 --> 00:45:32,430
With luck, she's dead in a ditch somewhere.

670
00:45:32,430 --> 00:45:33,940
Perhaps. But if not, we need her.

671
00:45:34,560 --> 00:45:36,800
They'll never give Jaime back to us for Sansa alone.

672
00:45:36,810 --> 00:45:38,780
I think they might. They're weak.

673
00:45:39,400 --> 00:45:41,210
They put too much value on their women.

674
00:45:42,260 --> 00:45:45,110
We need to set our armies to the task of finding her.

675
00:45:45,110 --> 00:45:46,800
Send out as many men as we can.

676
00:45:47,110 --> 00:45:48,920
I'm sure if you asked grandfather--

677
00:45:48,920 --> 00:45:52,160
The King does not ask; He commands.

678
00:45:53,230 --> 00:45:55,840
And my grandfather's stupidity in the field of battle

679
00:45:55,840 --> 00:45:58,400
is the reason Robb Stark has Uncle Jaime in the first place.

680
00:45:58,760 --> 00:46:00,500
His life is in danger.

681
00:46:01,430 --> 00:46:02,740
We're at war.

682
00:46:03,350 --> 00:46:04,800
All our lives are in danger.

683
00:46:09,080 --> 00:46:11,360
I heard a disgusting lie about Uncle Jaime

684
00:46:13,090 --> 00:46:13,850
and you.

685
00:46:15,670 --> 00:46:17,180
Our enemies will say anything

686
00:46:17,180 --> 00:46:18,740
to weaken your claim to the throne.

687
00:46:18,990 --> 00:46:20,950
It's not a claim. The throne is mine.

688
00:46:22,960 --> 00:46:23,970
Of course it is.

689
00:46:26,590 --> 00:46:29,310
- No one believes this foul gossip. - Someone believes it.

690
00:46:31,990 --> 00:46:33,630
Father had other children?

691
00:46:34,680 --> 00:46:36,800
Besides me and Tommen and Myrcella?

692
00:46:39,560 --> 00:46:40,860
What are you asking?

693
00:46:41,640 --> 00:46:43,490
I'm asking if he fucked other women

694
00:46:43,490 --> 00:46:44,910
when he grew tired of you.

695
00:46:44,910 --> 00:46:46,720
How many bastards does he have running--

696
00:47:02,800 --> 00:47:06,490
What you just did is punishable by death.

697
00:47:10,130 --> 00:47:11,480
You will never do it again.

698
00:47:13,250 --> 00:47:13,970
Never.

699
00:47:20,920 --> 00:47:22,240
That will be all, Mother.

700
00:47:29,630 --> 00:47:31,490
No, no, no, no.

701
00:47:31,490 --> 00:47:34,160
Do you have any idea how ridiculous you sound?

702
00:47:34,390 --> 00:47:36,130
Ease into it.

703
00:47:36,130 --> 00:47:38,630
Slowly, with passion.

704
00:47:41,620 --> 00:47:43,540
Oh, yeah.

705
00:47:44,270 --> 00:47:46,730
Go wash yourselves. Put some clothes on.

706
00:47:47,060 --> 00:47:48,850
Both of you are working tonight.

707
00:47:53,540 --> 00:47:55,370
We do things differently here, Daisy.

708
00:47:55,370 --> 00:47:59,360
This isn't some five-copper bawdy house in Hayseed Hall.

709
00:47:59,360 --> 00:48:01,510
- Haystack Hall. - Wherever you're from.

710
00:48:01,860 --> 00:48:03,860
Our establishment doesn't cater

711
00:48:03,860 --> 00:48:05,850
to ploughmen and goat herders.

712
00:48:06,680 --> 00:48:07,830
Lord Olsen.

713
00:48:08,800 --> 00:48:10,320
Taste is everything here.

714
00:48:10,580 --> 00:48:12,200
Littlefinger's a fancy man.

715
00:48:12,370 --> 00:48:13,800
Don't call him Littlefinger.

716
00:48:13,940 --> 00:48:15,110
He doesn't like it.

717
00:48:15,740 --> 00:48:17,110
Lord Baelish.

718
00:48:23,720 --> 00:48:26,170
She pretends she doesn't speak the common tongue

719
00:48:26,170 --> 00:48:27,960
so that people will think she's exotic.

720
00:48:28,590 --> 00:48:30,910
She grew up just down the road in Flea Bottom.

721
00:48:31,730 --> 00:48:33,220
She's beautiful.

722
00:48:33,770 --> 00:48:37,340
She's a dumb slut, really, but a lid for every pot.

723
00:48:42,280 --> 00:48:44,010
Lord Commander.

724
00:48:44,910 --> 00:48:47,010
Good to see you... Again.

725
00:49:02,720 --> 00:49:04,400
You do realize this establishment

726
00:49:04,400 --> 00:49:06,080
is owned by Lord Petyr Baelish,

727
00:49:06,550 --> 00:49:08,050
the King's Master of Coin...

728
00:49:08,920 --> 00:49:10,780
Coin which goes in many pockets.

729
00:49:11,330 --> 00:49:13,120
- Orders. - Whose orders?

730
00:49:13,360 --> 00:49:16,010
Someone who doesn't care what Littlefinger thinks.

731
00:49:34,430 --> 00:49:37,380
No, you can't. No! Please!

732
00:49:38,630 --> 00:49:40,860
No! Not my Barra!

733
00:49:41,040 --> 00:49:44,170
- Please. Please. - Enough. Get it done.

734
00:49:44,530 --> 00:49:46,240
- Kill the bastard. - No, no!

735
00:49:46,380 --> 00:49:48,660
- Please. - Give it here.

736
00:49:49,220 --> 00:49:50,860
No, please.

737
00:50:01,440 --> 00:50:03,500
Spread out. Search every house.

738
00:50:03,500 --> 00:50:05,460
Every room. Look in every room.

739
00:50:30,320 --> 00:50:32,990
Gendry! His name is Gendry.

740
00:50:32,990 --> 00:50:34,570
Where is the bastard?

741
00:50:34,820 --> 00:50:37,740
The Night's Watch! Please, stop!

742
00:50:37,740 --> 00:50:38,530
Where?

743
00:50:38,950 --> 00:50:41,770
They took him up the Kingsroad, heading north.

744
00:50:41,770 --> 00:50:43,090
How will we know him?

745
00:50:43,390 --> 00:50:47,040
He's got a bull's head helmet. He made it himself.

746
00:50:47,340 --> 00:50:48,480
Find him.

